Package: moonglow
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Thomas Martin <tmmuttathara@gmail.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1
Recommends: i2c-tools
Homepage: https://github.com/prompt-smithy/moonglow
Description: Desktop app for external-display brightness and scheduled colour temperature
 Moonglow drives external-monitor brightness over DDC/CI and
 follows a morning/evening colour-temperature schedule. Its settings window
 has brightness and colour-temperature sliders, a day/night range, global
 keyboard shortcuts, and a full command-line interface.
 .
 DDC/CI brightness needs i2c access: install i2c-tools, join the i2c group
 (sudo usermod -aG i2c $USER), and log out and back in.
